/// Three standard robustness checks for one specification.
///
/// The model with heteroskedasticity-robust standard errors, with errors clustered by
/// `cluster`, and with robust errors on the years from 2015 only, as a list of fits for
/// `report`. Fixed effects arrive with release 0.6.0, so the checks absorb none.
///
/// data: The frame to fit on; it needs a `year` variable.
/// f: The formula of the specification.
/// cluster: The variable to cluster by; the worker by default.
/// returns: The three fits, a List<RegFit>.
/// see also: reg, report
///
/// > len(dataset(wages).robustness(log(wage) ~ educ))
/// 3
fn robustness(data: Frame, f: Formula, cluster: Var = worker) -> List<RegFit> {
    [
        data.reg(f, se: robust),
        data.reg(f, cluster: cluster),
        data.where(year >= 2015).reg(f, se: robust),
    ]
}
